    {
        "id": "e8004d6c147a853a",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "ee5baa48c91ec01d",
        "name": "SAFETY / commissioning notes",
        "info": "This flow is an example integration and must be tested with the motors mechanically disabled or safely isolated first. \nThe dashboard STOP button is NOT an emergency stop. Keep a hardwired safety circuit. In the supplied Arduino code, \nhandleTCPClient() blocks in a while(client.connected()) loop, which can delay polling the physical stop/E-stop \ninputs while connected. Fix that firmware behavior before live operation. The RELEASE_TO_AUTO command switches \nto AUTO_CYCLE in the supplied code; verify this behavior is intended before using the button. TCP request behavior \nand response timeout must be verified against your installed Node-RED version and P1AM firmware.",
        "x": 790,
        "y": 680,
        "wires": []
    },
